  "notes": "The PDF parse on a Kaggle T4. VCB Q1-2026 is the test case because all three of its statements already read `pdf` at `onnx@200` on this machine, from the consolidated filing - so the run has an exact baseline and `compare()` scores every cell against it. The question is NOT whether the quarter parses (it does, here); it is whether a T4 with Kaggle's own torch and onnxruntime reproduces the same LAYER and the same FIGURES. Run 1 (2026-08-28, 83.8 s) reproduced all 98 cells - and its log showed DB detection had fallen back to the CPU, because a bare `onnxruntime-gpu` resolves to 1.29.0 which needs CUDA 13 against Kaggle's 12.8. onnxruntime-gpu is pinned to the CUDA 12 line (1.20.1, this repo's own version) and the notebook now reports what the SESSION holds rather than what get_available_providers() advertises. Nothing is written back to the statement CSVs either way.",
